    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194-a3">

                <pb facs="0475" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg379"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    107.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, in reverting to his note of 29th April, has the honor to inform
                    Mr. H. Sidney Everett, chargé d’affaires of the United States of America, that
                    he has just received a communication from the proper authorities to the effect
                    that the wish expressed in a note of 23d April, that the time of military
                    service of the servant Wilhelm Knoth may be diminished, cannot under existing
                    laws be complied with.</p>
                <p>The undersigned has also the honor to state that the time of service of said
                    Knoth expires to-day, and to avail himself of this occasion to renew the
                    assurance of his most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">von</hi> BÜLOW.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
